Rule 1 (disallow complex dtypes for tensor-tensor comparison)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 3 (broadcastable shapes when both tensors have the same rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 7 (out shape matches broadcast result when ranks are equal)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ((shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)))
>>
Rule 9 (right-aligned broadcasting when input has more dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) = 1
>>
Rule 10 (right-aligned broadcasting when other has more dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) > ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) = 1
